We consider the following non-autonomous obstacle problem:
$$
\left\{
\begin{array}{ll}
\min \left\{ |Du|^p(x) + u(x)\cdot Du(x) - \Delta_u u(x), \psi(x) \right\} = 0, & x \in \Omega, \\
u(x) = u_0(x), & x \in \Omega^c,
\end{array}
\right.
$$
where $\Omega \subseteq \mathbb{R}^n$ is an open and bounded domain, $p > 1$, $\Delta_u u(x)$ is the uniformly parabolic operator defined as $\sum_{i=1}^n \partial_i (|Du(x)|^{p-2} \partial_i u(x))$, and $u_0(x)$ is the given extension of $\psi(x)$ outside of $\Omega$. Under the condition that $u_0(x)$ is Hölder continuous, we prove that the solution $u(x)$ is also Hölder continuous. Additionally, we establish the existence of a $C^{1,\alpha}$ regular region for the solution $u(x)$.
